                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa2b1a72-50a2-3a56-ba2c-d2e844a04578",
                        "entry_id": "632c2d0e-1fd5-302e-a355-98a74929c03e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dreadful; disturbing or frightening."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8789b797-9543-4f0d-aba7-d176182e27d0",
                                "sense_id": "fa2b1a72-50a2-3a56-ba2c-d2e844a04578",
                                "text": "And when I signified my intention of making a tour of the whole province, they most earnestly advised me to alter my plans, and occupy my time in visiting some other part of the kingdom; for they assured me, that all travellers who attempted Basse Bretagne, returned in disgust before they went more thant a few stages into the country, for that its general aspect was that of desolation itself; the roads were impassable ; and the people dirty, ragged barbarians, living in filthy huts, and clothed in sheepskins; that, in short, everything was affreux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65480bb0-c2eb-4e02-aa96-23ecc6c54550",
                                "sense_id": "fa2b1a72-50a2-3a56-ba2c-d2e844a04578",
                                "text": "It was in rain that some common friends represented the tort affreux — the frightful mischief he would do the government of his own creation, if he published this work — all in vain: his honor, his conscience, and his patriotism, required that he should raise his voice in defence of the charter, which the king and his ministers equally violate — and the work is published!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6296b52b-b5d5-42ca-965c-2fdf3ae0fa96",
                                "sense_id": "fa2b1a72-50a2-3a56-ba2c-d2e844a04578",
                                "text": "Orpheus calls the sound 'affreux'; the examiners may have agreed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af283707-2107-46c3-99fe-682fd75b1543",
                                "sense_id": "fa2b1a72-50a2-3a56-ba2c-d2e844a04578",
                                "text": "No doubt they would be talking about the affreux – dreadful – Germans. Not so affreux, of course, that one refused to get rich off them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66e4eb41-58f6-4826-b7c8-a3b67e84bd30",
                                "sense_id": "fa2b1a72-50a2-3a56-ba2c-d2e844a04578",
                                "text": "As soon as they were in the courtyard, she whispered, “M. Hoffmann has just appeared looking affreux. And he brought with him his father of all things!”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "5ca16fea-478c-33fd-933e-10844a14b9c6",
                "word": "affreux",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ae30a13-16de-3085-bd0d-2334b1b5729b",
                        "entry_id": "5ca16fea-478c-33fd-933e-10844a14b9c6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A group of particularly brutal mercenaries who were active in Africa and Asia during the 1960s."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0688848-3ce5-4e73-92b0-7469d9ad0cba",
                                "sense_id": "3ae30a13-16de-3085-bd0d-2334b1b5729b",
                                "text": "As one Belgian journalist wrote: The affreux [\"frightful ones\"] are outstanding in combat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "faab2041-fcb3-497e-b0be-005f780eca71",
                                "sense_id": "3ae30a13-16de-3085-bd0d-2334b1b5729b",
                                "text": "I could no longer find anything affected in that long smooth white face but an extreme kindness and a sort of obstinate candour; Vian was as Herv in his detestation of the affreux [the frightful ones] as in loving what he loved."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6d77d33-bab3-4c66-b987-43895ecf0789",
                                "sense_id": "3ae30a13-16de-3085-bd0d-2334b1b5729b",
                                "text": "These were mostly, but not exclusively, members of the Baluba tribe and had fled the persecution of Munongo's mercenary affreux and their black rank-and-file."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77b2ef4d-229d-4dbe-ba3d-44ea5ca67de4",
                                "sense_id": "3ae30a13-16de-3085-bd0d-2334b1b5729b",
                                "text": "It takes a rather wilful ignorance to refuse to recognize the essential difference between, say, the affreux of mid-twentieth-century Africa and the Royal Gurkha Rifles, though both could loosely be described as mercenaries."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3af74602-c418-48fb-9374-49994b61c305",
                                "sense_id": "3ae30a13-16de-3085-bd0d-2334b1b5729b",
                                "text": "He had once been one of the dreaded affreux, the “frightful ones,” the white freelance soldiers who helped keep dictators in power throughout Africa and Asia."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa92e9c9-8364-4770-8207-bec57d4e472d",
                                "sense_id": "3ae30a13-16de-3085-bd0d-2334b1b5729b",
                                "text": "France's return to Comoros was, above all, conspicuous through the actions of the mercenary leader Bob Denard and his team of affreux ('dreadful')."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
